B = [
('Supermarine','Europe','1930s-40s','aircraft','In the style of Supermarine, sleek, purposeful British aerodynamic purity of the 1930s and 1940s. Graceful elliptical curves, long slim volumes, tapering ends and a narrow stance, all in polished metal skin with flush, tidy rivets. Colour is either dark green and earth brown shading to pale sky blue, or glossy blue and silver lacquer. Bright round markings in red, white and blue give crisp contrast. Fine, thin lines and smooth rounded transparent forms. Fast-looking, elegant, lean and precise, pared down to speed alone.'),
('Cessna','North America','1960s-70s','aircraft','In the style of Cessna, friendly, simple, practical design from the 1960s and 1970s. Boxy but approachable white forms with softened corners, generous wraparound windows and plain, honest shapes that are easy to read. Painted sweeping side stripes in red, blue, gold or green add a note of optimism, with small neat numerals as the only lettering. Sturdy, unfussy, utility-first and casual, with a weekend-adventure cheerfulness and clean enamel finish.'),
('Sikorsky','North America','1950s-70s','helicopters','In the style of Sikorsky, rugged, heavy-duty, utilitarian machinery. Big rounded, bulbous masses with deep glazing, stubby add-on volumes and a long tapering tail. Riveted aluminium skin with visible fasteners and panel seams. Colour is either matte olive drab and grey, or white and red for rescue, with big black and white stencilled numbers and warnings. No ornament, everything functional, strong, workmanlike and built to lift and endure.'),
('Concorde','Europe','1970s','aircraft','In the style of Concorde, needle-sharp, supersonic, futuristic elegance of the 1970s. A tall, slender white form narrowing to a long pointed tip, with tiny oval windows set in a slim line. A pure, smooth, sweeping triangular outline tapers back into a narrow end. White paint is relieved only by one thin blue line. Knife-slim, bird-like, pared-back and aerodynamic, with a refined, rarefied air of speed and luxury.'),
('Kenworth','North America','1970s-present','trucks','In the style of Kenworth, proud, polished, long-nosed American heavy-duty highway presence. Tall, upright, mirror-bright chrome faces, bold chrome edge strips and heavy chrome bars set against deep two-tone paint split by a confident stripe. Round lamps, tall stainless columns and polished aluminium accents. Proportions are long, flat and roomy with a commanding stance. Everything is gleaming, mirrored and meticulously cared for, bold and confident, king-of-the-road.'),
('Peterbilt','North America','1970s-present','trucks','In the style of Peterbilt, a showy, sculpted, long-nosed American heavy-duty look. Long, curved forms with bold oval chrome shapes, vertical slatted detailing, rounded corners and single round chrome-ringed lights. Tall chrome columns, big chrome bars and polished metal covers. Brilliant candy paint in black, red, blue or green is trimmed with fine pinstripes and gold lines. Classic, bold, polished and proud, with a strong stance and lots of mirror-bright metal.'),
('Scania','Europe','2000s-present','trucks','In the style of Scania, clean, crisp, modern Nordic engineering with a tall, flat-fronted, upright face. Broad forms crossed by one bold horizontal bar, narrow angular lights and wide, tall glazing. Rounded upper forms, long smooth skirts and tidy lines that flow back along the body. A small silver and blue crowned winged-beast emblem sits centred. Colour is tidy and solid, in white, red, blue or yellow, with no clutter. Rational, safe, practical and quietly premium.'),
('Mack Trucks','North America','1950s-present','trucks','In the style of Mack Trucks, blunt, tough, muscular American heavy-duty character. A bulldog-like, forward-thrust mass, a top line that curves down steeply and a bold chrome standing animal ornament. Stout upright chrome faces with horizontal bars, round chrome lamps, short heavy curves and thick chrome bars. Bright enamel in red, yellow, blue or black, with stainless accents. Chunky, compact, solid and no-nonsense, proportioned like a determined fighter, with polished highlights on a hard-working frame.'),
('John Deere','North America','1950s-present','tractors','In the style of John Deere, robust, hard-working, clean agricultural design. Deep green bodywork with bright yellow trim, forming one memorable two-colour pairing. Boxy forms with vertical slatted detailing, rounded caps and a tall column accent. A bold leaping deer mark in yellow serves as the single emblem. Simple yellow stripes and clean decals accent the green. Practical proportions, honest function, tidy, dependable and rooted in the countryside.'),
('Fendt','Europe','2000s-present','tractors','In the style of Fendt, premium, precise German farm engineering in glossy, bright lime green with matte black accents. High-polish paint, sleek rounded lines and sharply cut angular strips of light. Large glass areas with curved panoramic sweep, metallic silver and black faces with one wide horizontal slot, and minimal clutter across clean, tight bodywork. Exact panel gaps suggest sharp machining. Modern, upmarket, tidy, high-tech and confident, like agricultural luxury.'),
('Massey Ferguson','Europe','1950s-70s','tractors','In the style of Massey Ferguson, plain, sturdy post-war farm machinery. Bright red bodywork with grey structural parts, a rounded top line with vertical slatted detailing and chunky, honest forms. Exposed mechanical parts and simple open arrangements, with bold block lettering. Two strong colours, red and grey, are used flat and simply with no gradients. Honest, tough, utilitarian, no frills, and rooted in mid-century working farmland.'),
('Routemaster','Europe','1950s-60s','buses','In the style of Routemaster, nostalgic, rounded, sturdy London transport design. Deep pillar-box red paint with a cream or pale band dividing the levels, boxy forms with big curved corners and a tall rounded front. Open, welcoming arrangements with simple metal poles, a circular roundel mark and deep sliding windows. Numbers use stencil-like, bold lettering. Civic, familiar, friendly and proudly old-fashioned.'),
('Greyhound','North America','1950s-60s','buses','In the style of Greyhound, optimistic mid-century American road-travel streamlining. Stainless steel bodies with long fluted, corrugated sides, a low rounded top and large tinted windows. A leaping dog silhouette appears as the single emblem. Colour is blue and silver with white stripes. Polished aluminium panels, rounded edges and a smooth, speed-minded profile. Shiny, practical, spacious, modern-for-its-time and full of highway confidence.'),
('Great Western Railway','Europe','1930s','railways','In the style of Great Western Railway, proud Victorian-inspired engineering elegance. Gleaming deep green paint with orange and black lining, polished brass and copper accents, black dark-toned ends and red bases. Tall brass-edged nameplates sit on curved forms. Secondary colours are cream and chocolate brown. Metal is hand-polished, lines are fine and hand-drawn, and every part is crafted to be admired. Stately, dignified, traditional and richly finished.'),
('Shinkansen','East Asia','1960s-present','railways','In the style of Shinkansen, calm, ultra-precise, aerodynamic Japanese high-speed modernity. A long, smooth, continuous form ending in a duck-bill or beak-shaped tip, with rounded cross-sections and flush windows and doors. White bodywork carries one thin blue or colour stripe. Narrow wraparound glazing, low skirts hiding working parts, and near-seamless, polished surfaces. Quiet, futuristic, tidy and disciplined, where every curve serves speed and silence.'),
('TGV','Europe','1980s','railways','In the style of TGV, sleek, French, wedge-shaped, high-speed modernism of the 1980s. Pointed, sloped fronts, a long tapering top line and a tightly joined slim body. Colour is orange and silver-grey, with a bold orange lower band and a dark grey upper area. Windows are flush, surfaces are smooth, and the profile is low, streamlined and futuristic. Confident, athletic, sporty, sharply tailored and engineered for speed.'),
('Orient Express','Europe','1920s-30s','railways','In the style of Orient Express, opulent, romantic 1920s-30s luxury travel. Deep royal blue panels with gold lettering and fine gold lining, rounded barrel-vaulted forms and polished brass rails. Interiors glow with glossy varnished teak and mahogany, marquetry panels, burgundy velvet, crisp white linen, crystal and silver. Art deco lamps have frosted glass tulip shades. Everything is lacquered, gilded and carefully made. Atmosphere is glamorous, intimate, mysterious and unhurried.'),
('Riva','Europe','1960s','boats','In the style of Riva, glamorous, glossy Italian Riviera luxury of the 1960s. Long, slim, low forms in deep mahogany, with varnished surfaces in bright caramel grain, finished to mirror gloss. Curved, polished chrome frames and fittings, white leather or cream and red upholstery, and fine white or gold pinstripes. Swept lines, rounded curves and small neat flourishes. Handmade, sensual, sleek, sunlit and richly refined, with a jet-set summer feel.'),
('Chris-Craft','North America','1930s-50s','boats','In the style of Chris-Craft, classic, varnished, lakeside summer glamour in the 1930s-50s American tradition. Rich red-brown mahogany planking polished to a deep shine, with fine white seams between boards. Chrome-framed glazing, chrome fittings, slim tapering lines and rounded ends with flowing script lettering. Tufted leather in red and cream and neatly curved enclosures. Handcrafted, warm, nostalgic, sporty and carefree, like long sunny weekends on calm water.'),
('Sunseeker','Europe','2000s-present','boats','In the style of Sunseeker, sleek, low, sporty British luxury. A raked, aggressive forward slope, long white glossy surfaces and dark tinted wraparound glazing. Bold swooping stripes sweep along the sides, with polished stainless details and teak-clad surfaces. Interiors are lacquered in cream leather and high-gloss wood. Speed-minded, status-conscious, polished and flamboyant, with a high-glamour resort look and a cool white palette.'),
('Boston Whaler','North America','1960s-present','boats','In the style of Boston Whaler, honest, tough, practical, unsinkable simplicity. Wide, stable, sturdy forms in white gelcoat with a thin navy or blue stripe low on the sides and a high flared front. Simple central arrangements with polished stainless details, grey non-slip surfaces and neat bolted-on fittings. No fuss, no ornament, durable, utilitarian, ready for work or play, with a straightforward coastal feel.'),
('NASA','North America','1960s-70s','spacecraft','In the style of NASA, clean, technical, optimistic American spaceflight of the 1960s and 1970s. Tall white forms with bold black patterns, small flags in red, white and blue, and golden foil-wrapped shapes. Bright white surfaces with orange or silver details. Marks are either a red, worm-like lettering or a blue circle with stars and a swoosh. Riveted aluminium panels, dark glossy surfaces, exposed cabling and bell shapes, all against black space. Engineered, heroic, hopeful and precise.'),
('SpaceX','North America','2010s-present','spacecraft','In the style of SpaceX, minimalist, gleaming, modern reusable spaceflight. Smooth white cylinders with clean bold finishes, or polished bare stainless steel, with slender black accents. Lower areas are sooty and streaked with carbon from fiery returns. Rounded tips, slim grid shapes and minimal bold sans-serif lettering. Few marks, no ornament, only function. Sleek, futuristic, confident, utilitarian and quietly daring.'),
('Soviet space programme','Russia and Eastern Europe','1960s','spacecraft','In the style of Soviet space programme, blunt, heavy, utilitarian 1960s industrial heroism. Round spherical forms with small round openings, bare pea green and metallic silver surfaces, tapering volumes clustered around a central core, and brushed orange-tinted foil. White sections carry stencilled numbers, with bold red capital lettering and a red star mark. Visible cables, rivets and welded seams. Raw, practical, monumental, heavy-engineered and undecorated, with a stern, proud Cold War mood.'),
('Pullman','North America','1900s-30s','railways','In the style of Pullman, formal Gilded Age elegance in luxury travel of the early 1900s. Deep dark green paint with elaborate gold-leaf lettering and lines, arched forms with small high windows and open railings. Interiors in walnut with green or burgundy plush upholstery, brass fittings and gaslight-style lamps. Heavy, solid, stately forms. Ornate, rich, ceremonial, hand-gilded and imposing, like a rolling grand hotel.'),
('Piaggio Ape','Europe','1950s-60s','trucks','In the style of Piaggio Ape, tiny, quaint, cheerful Italian village practicality. Rounded compact forms, simple basic controls and small tin utility shapes. Pressed-steel body in pastel mint, cream, light blue or sun-faded yellow, with soft rounded curves, tiny glazing and chrome trim around a single round lamp. Simple, humble, charming, slightly worn and friendly, built for narrow lanes and daily errands.'),
('Zeppelin','Europe','1920s-30s','aircraft','In the style of Zeppelin, stately, monumental, silver-giant 1920s-30s elegance. An enormous cigar-shaped form stretched taut over a light frame, covered in silvery metallic cloth, with a small streamlined volume beneath and neat rows of windows. Cruciform tail shapes and bold black angular lettering along the length, plus a red accent at the rear. Smooth, gleaming, serene and huge, with a majestic, floating, slow-moving presence and a dignified period grandeur.'),
('Bajaj Auto','South Asia','1970s-1990s','vehicles','In the style of Bajaj Auto, cheerful, unpretentious, resilient and familiar, packed with colour on a dusty street. Rounded pressed-steel bodies with bulbous curves, vinyl-covered seating and chrome badges. Thick glossy enamel in sky blue, cream, off-white, rust red and olive green, with round chrome-rimmed lamps and stubby upright details. Tiny compact forms with canvas or sheet metal enclosures, open sides, lemon yellow and black or green and yellow pairings, painted slogans and plastic flower garlands.'),
('Proton','Southeast Asia','1980s-2000s','cars','In the style of Proton, proud, modest, practical, optimistic national design of the 1980s and 1990s. Compact, boxy, upright volumes with flat sides, a straight shoulder line, slim chrome edging, rectangular shapes and plain black panels carrying a small badge. Emblems are a dark blue shield with a yellow crescent and star, or a yellow tiger head in a green roundel. Paint is solid gloss in white, red, silver, dark blue and champagne gold, with black plastic trim. Plain grey cloth textures. Sunlit and unpretentious.'),
('Dona Rosa Barro Negro','Latin America','1950s-present','ceramics','In the style of Dona Rosa Barro Negro, hand-built forms with a deep, mirror-like metallic black sheen. Shapes are formed by hand with no turning, so they are softly rounded and slightly asymmetrical, with tall proportions, round bellies, narrow necks and playful figure shapes. The surface is rubbed smooth with a stone before smoke firing, giving a silky gunmetal-to-jet shine with soft grey matte patches where the burnish is lighter. Decoration is restrained, with applied flowers, rosettes, twisted ropes, delicate pierced lacework and fine incised lines. Earthy, sculptural and quietly elegant, on plain pale backgrounds.'),
]
